ROOT=(Path(__file__).resolve().parent/'dist')
lessons=[]
def L(ch,a,b,title,mental,core,decision,trap,example,question,answer):
 lessons.append(dict(id=f'l{len(lessons)+1:03}',chapter=ch,start=a,end=b,title=title,mental=mental,core=core.split('~'),decision=decision,trap=trap,example=example,question=question,answer=answer))
L(0,1,8,'How to think like a Professional architect','SAP-C02 menguji pilihan terbaik di bawah constraints. Mengenal nama service saja belum cukup.','Read the business objective first: minimum downtime, least operational effort, lowest cost, or strict isolation.~Then identify hard constraints: protocol, engine compatibility, data residency, RPO/RTO, throughput, permissions, and team capacity.~Eliminate any answer that violates one hard constraint, even if its service is generally excellent. Compare the remaining options against the stated priority.','Use a five-step routine: objective → constraints → mechanism → eliminate → trade-off.','A familiar architecture is not automatically the best answer. “Managed” also does not mean you have no configuration responsibility.','A Windows application cannot simply move to Graviton because Graviton uses Arm processors and software compatibility matters.','Two answers work. How do you choose?','Choose the one that meets every hard requirement and best satisfies the explicit optimization goal. Explain why the runner-up is worse.')
L(1,9,15,'IAM policies: who can do what?','IAM = daftar izin. Principal adalah pihak yang meminta; action adalah kegiatan; resource adalah objek; condition adalah syarat.','Users can have long-lived credentials. Roles provide temporary credentials through STS. Groups organize users; roles are assumed, not joined.~A policy statement has Effect, Action/NotAction, Resource and optional Condition. Explicit deny wins. An absent allow is an implicit deny.~Managed policies can be reused; inline policies belong to one identity. Variables and principal/resource tags support ABAC.','Use least privilege and roles for workloads. Conditions narrow a permission by context such as TLS, source network, region, tags or MFA.','NotAction inside an Allow is not an explicit Deny. Another policy may allow an excluded action. Do not hard-code the changing contents of AWS managed policies.','Allow GetObject on reports/* plus Deny GetObject on reports/payroll/* means payroll remains denied. ListBucket needs the bucket ARN; object operations need an object ARN.','Does PowerUserAccess express an explicit denial of every IAM action?','No. Its Allow with NotAction excludes actions from that statement. Read all policies and any explicit denies.')
L(1,16,21,'Roles, resource policies & permission ceilings','Role = ganti kartu akses. Resource policy = pemilik pintu mengizinkan principal tertentu masuk. Boundary = batas maksimum.','Assuming a role creates a new session whose effective permissions come from the role and applicable restrictions; original user permissions are not added.~A resource policy is attached to a bucket, queue, key or other supported resource. Cross-account access normally needs permission on both sides.~A permissions boundary limits an identity; it grants nothing. Access Analyzer finds external access, validates policies and can generate policies from observed activity.','Use a boundary when delegating IAM creation. Use a resource policy when granting access to a resource without switching the caller into a new role.','Resource-policy behavior differs for user ARNs, role ARNs and assumed-role session ARNs. The simple “intersect everything” model is not universal; explicit denies still apply.','An analyst reads DynamoDB in account A and writes to S3 in B using its A role plus B bucket policy, avoiding an unnecessary role switch.','Can a boundary by itself grant s3:GetObject?','No. It only limits permissions granted elsewhere. The appropriate allow and every applicable policy check are still required.')
L(1,22,29,'STS, cross-account access & confused deputy','STS = loket yang menerbitkan kartu akses sementara. Trust policy menjawab siapa boleh assume role.','AssumeRole needs a role trust relationship and caller authorization. The returned access key, secret key and session token belong together.~For a third-party provider serving many customers, require a unique ExternalId in the trust policy. The provider supplies the customer-specific value when assuming the role.~AssumeRoleWithSAML and AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity exchange federation assertions/tokens. Session tags carry attributes into authorization.','Deploy least-privilege monitoring roles to member accounts with StackSets. Trust the provider account and require its ExternalId.','ExternalId is not a password or secret. Its purpose is preventing customer A from tricking a provider into accessing customer B. Role chaining has a one-hour session limit.','A vendor knows many customer role ARNs. AWS checks both its principal and the ExternalId, binding the request to the intended customer.','Why is trusting only the vendor account insufficient?','All of that vendor’s customer requests may originate from the same account. ExternalId distinguishes the customer on whose behalf it acts.')
L(1,30,38,'Federation: SAML, OIDC & Cognito','Federation = login di identity provider, lalu AWS mempercayai bukti login tersebut. Tidak perlu IAM user per orang.','SAML 2.0 commonly federates enterprise identities. STS AssumeRoleWithSAML returns temporary credentials for API access; console federation adds AWS sign-in redirection.~OIDC uses web identity tokens. Cognito user pools authenticate application users and issue JWTs; identity pools exchange supported identity tokens for temporary AWS credentials.~A custom identity broker authenticates with a legacy identity system and obtains scoped temporary credentials when standard federation is unavailable.','Workforce across AWS accounts: IAM Identity Center. Customer application login: Cognito user pool. Customer direct S3 access: identity pool plus role permissions.','A user-pool JWT is not an AWS access key. Direct OIDC federation also has valid workload uses; “always use Cognito” is too broad.','A mobile app signs in to a user pool, presents its JWT to API Gateway, or uses an identity pool for restricted direct uploads to a user prefix.','Which Cognito pool gives AWS credentials?','Identity pools. User pools primarily provide application authentication and tokens.')
L(1,39,47,'Active Directory: managed, proxy, or basic?','AD menyimpan identitas dan domain objects. ADFS menerbitkan federation assertions. Keduanya punya tugas berbeda.','AWS Managed Microsoft AD supplies managed domain controllers, multi-AZ availability and supported integrations such as domain join and RDS SQL Server. Trust can connect it to on-premises AD.~AD Connector proxies authentication to existing on-premises AD. It does not cache credentials or create a new directory replica; connectivity remains a dependency.~Simple AD is a smaller Samba-based compatible directory without Microsoft AD’s full feature set or forest trust.','Need Microsoft AD features/trust: Managed Microsoft AD. Keep identities only on premises and proxy authentication: AD Connector. Basic standalone compatibility: Simple AD.','A forest trust does not copy users. AD Connector does not keep authentication working through a lost on-premises connection.','For resilient AD access, plan DNS, network redundancy and domain-controller availability; merely creating a trust does not remove network dependencies.','Trust versus replication: what changes?','Trust permits authentication across domains. Replication copies directory data among appropriate domain controllers.')
L(1,48,54,'Organizations & multi-account structure','AWS account adalah isolation boundary untuk resources, permissions, billing attribution, dan banyak quotas. OU mengelompokkan accounts.','Separate production, development, security and log archive accounts according to risk and ownership. OUs organize common controls.~Organizations supports consolidated billing and all-features governance. Discount sharing can pool eligible RI and Savings Plans benefits; it can also be disabled.~OrganizationAccountAccessRole is created for accounts created through Organizations; invited accounts need an appropriate role established separately. Moving an account requires leaving/removal from its current organization before joining another.','Use accounts for strong workload/administrative isolation; use VPCs for network separation inside an account. Centralize logs in a dedicated account.','Consolidated billing does not grant cross-account resource access. A management-account role is not automatically an administrator of every resource in every member account.','Finance receives one bill, while production operators and development operators retain separate role assignments and account quotas.','Why not put every team in one account with separate VPCs?','VPCs separate networks, but they do not provide the same IAM, billing and account-level quota boundaries as separate accounts.')
L(1,55,64,'SCPs, tags & organization policies','SCP = pagar organisasi. IAM masih harus memberikan izin di dalam pagar itu.','SCPs constrain member-account principals, including their root users. They do not constrain the management account or service-linked roles.~An allow must survive every level along the OU path; an explicit deny at any applicable level blocks access. Use aws:RequestedRegion carefully because global services need exceptions.~Tag policies standardize supported tags; enforce required tag presence with suitable request-tag conditions/SCPs. Organization backup and AI opt-out policies centralize their respective settings.','Use preventive controls for prohibited actions. Use tag policies for consistency and separate checks for missing required tags.','ForAllValues on aws:TagKeys validates supplied keys; it does not prove every required tag exists. Missing-value/Null conditions matter. Tag policies do not universally stop untagged resources.','A developer has AdministratorAccess, but a parent OU denies ec2:RunInstances outside approved Regions. The launch fails.','Does attaching FullAWSAccess as an SCP grant admin access?','No. It removes that SCP restriction; an identity still needs its own permissions.')
L(1,65,69,'IAM Identity Center & permission sets','Satu workforce login, akses berbeda untuk setiap AWS account. Permission set adalah paket izin yang diprovisikan menjadi role.','Connect an identity source: built-in directory, supported external IdP or AD. Assign users/groups to accounts with permission sets.~The same engineer can have ReadOnly in production and Administrator in a sandbox. Attribute-based access control can map workforce attributes to session tags.~Application assignments enable SAML application access; they are distinct from permissions to AWS resources.','Choose Identity Center for centralized workforce access across accounts. Use roles for machine-to-machine vendor access.','Sharing a human username/password with a monitoring vendor is a poor machine identity design. A permission set must be assigned to the right account and principal.','Group Developers receives DeveloperAccess in Dev and ReadOnly in Prod; Operators receives a separate production operations permission set.','What is the difference between identity source and permission set?','The source authenticates who you are; the permission set determines the AWS access you receive in assigned accounts.')
L(1,70,73,'Control Tower: a governed landing zone','Landing zone = lingkungan AWS awal yang sudah punya struktur accounts, logging, identity, dan controls.','Control Tower orchestrates a governed multi-account environment on top of Organizations. Account Factory automates account provisioning with approved baselines.~Preventive controls stop actions, detective controls report noncompliance, and proactive controls can check supported resources before provisioning.~Mandatory, strongly recommended and elective describe guidance levels, not whether a control is preventive or detective.','Choose Control Tower when asked to quickly establish and consistently govern a new multi-account environment.','AWS Config detecting a violation is not the same as an SCP blocking it. Account Factory provisions baselines; it does not design every application.','A new project account inherits logging and organization controls automatically instead of a team manually rebuilding them each time.','Which control can stop a prohibited API action before it happens?','An appropriate preventive control such as an SCP. Detective Config rules evaluate state after creation/change.')
L(1,74,79,'RAM: share infrastructure without merging ownership','RAM = berbagi resource yang didukung, bukan berbagi semua izin atau semua data dalam account.','VPC subnet sharing lets participant accounts launch their own resources into centrally managed subnets. Network owners manage routing; participants retain ownership of their resources.~Share supported resources such as Transit Gateways, Resolver rules, managed prefix lists and private CAs to reduce duplication.~Customer-managed prefix lists group CIDRs, letting one maintained list feed multiple security rules. Sharing Resolver rules centralizes hybrid DNS forwarding.','Use RAM when the requirement says shared subnets, shared TGW or common DNS rules across accounts.','Connectivity still depends on route tables, security groups and NACLs. Shared subnet does not mean unrestricted access or ownership of another account’s instances.','A networking account owns subnets and TGW; app accounts deploy services into shared subnets and manage only their own workloads.','RAM or Organizations for consolidated billing?','Organizations handles consolidated billing. RAM shares supported resources.')
L(2,80,92,'CloudTrail: who changed it?','CloudTrail adalah audit trail API activity. CloudWatch menjawab kesehatan; Config menjawab konfigurasi.','Management events describe control-plane changes such as launching EC2. Data events describe supported resource-level operations such as S3 GetObject and require appropriate configuration.~Event history provides recent management events. Trails or other configured storage support longer retention; central multi-account logging needs the right destination policies.~Use EventBridge for event-driven reactions, CloudWatch metric filters for repeated patterns, and S3/Athena for durable analysis. Integrity validation detects tampering; Object Lock can protect retention.','Deleted resource or suspicious API action: CloudTrail. Organization-wide audit retention: organization trail plus a protected log archive.','CloudTrail is not a SQL query log, packet capture or hard real-time prevention system. A trail and 90-day event history are not the same feature.','An alarm counts repeated denied API calls; responders inspect the initiating role and source context in CloudTrail.','How do you audit S3 object downloads?','Configure relevant S3 object data events. Default management-event history alone is insufficient.')
L(2,93,101,'KMS & envelope encryption','Envelope encryption = kunci data mengenkripsi data; KMS key melindungi kunci data itu.','Customer-managed keys offer policies, lifecycle control and auditing. AWS managed and AWS owned keys give progressively less customer control.~Imported key material keeps external material-management responsibilities with you. A custom key store uses your CloudHSM cluster. Key origin and algorithm affect supported rotation features.~Related multi-Region keys share key material and key ID but have regional ARNs, policies and independent regional management. Services do not automatically become globally replicated because their keys are related.','Use a customer-managed key when cross-account sharing or custom controls are required. Check both IAM permissions and key policy.','S3 read permission does not imply kms:Decrypt. Key rotation does not re-encrypt every existing object; old ciphertext must remain decryptable.','An S3 reader in account B needs the bucket/object permission and permission to decrypt with the customer-managed key in A.','Does a multi-Region KMS key replicate my S3 objects?','No. It addresses cryptographic interoperability; configure data replication independently.')
L(2,102,110,'Parameter Store vs Secrets Manager','Parameter = konfigurasi. Secret = nilai sensitif yang perlu lifecycle dan sering perlu rotation.','Parameter Store provides hierarchical names, versions and optional SecureString encryption. Advanced parameter policies include expiration and notifications; expiration is not password rotation.~Secrets Manager provides managed secret storage, resource policies and supported rotation workflows. Rotating a database secret must coordinate the stored value and the database password.~A secret injected into a container environment at startup is a snapshot. Rotation does not magically rewrite running process variables.','Simple configuration: Parameter Store. Database credentials requiring managed rotation: Secrets Manager. Cross-account secret access: resource policy plus KMS permissions.','Encrypting a value is not rotating it. A cached or injected secret can become stale after rotation.','Store /shop/prod/api-url as a parameter and the production database password as a rotating secret. Refresh clients or redeploy tasks as needed.','Why can a container fail after successful secret rotation?','Its environment may still contain the old credential. Applications must refresh secrets or tasks must be replaced.')
L(2,111,118,'TLS, certificates, SNI & ACM','TLS melindungi data saat bergerak. Sertifikat membuktikan identitas server; encryption at rest melindungi penyimpanan.','Modern TLS negotiates symmetric session keys using secure handshake mechanisms. Validate the certificate chain and hostname; using HTTPS while trusting a malicious certificate defeats protection.~SNI tells the server which hostname the client wants, allowing multiple certificates on a listener.~ACM manages certificates for supported integrations. CloudFront viewer certificates belong in us-east-1; regional load balancers use regional certificates. Imported certificates require renewal handling.','Terminate TLS at ALB for managed certificate integration; use HTTPS to targets too when end-to-end encryption is required.','DNSSEC authenticates DNS data; it does not encrypt application traffic. The deck’s legacy RSA handshake is not a universal description of modern TLS.','shop.example.com and api.example.com share an ALB HTTPS listener with SNI choosing the relevant certificate.','Does TLS termination on ALB guarantee encryption to EC2?','No. Configure HTTPS between ALB and targets if that leg must also be encrypted.')
L(2,119,126,'CloudHSM & TLS architecture','CloudHSM memberi dedicated hardware cryptography dengan tanggung jawab key/user administration di pihak kamu.','KMS is managed key usage through AWS APIs and policies. CloudHSM offers dedicated HSMs and cryptographic interfaces for applications with specific control requirements.~Deploy HSMs across AZs for availability. Applications need supported client integration and cryptographic-user access, not just IAM permission to create a cluster.~TLS offload can keep private-key operations inside the HSM while servers handle application traffic.','Choose CloudHSM when dedicated HSM control or specific cryptographic interfaces are mandatory. Choose KMS for simpler service-integrated key management.','Buying one HSM does not produce multi-AZ resilience. Also, CloudHSM user credentials and IAM administration solve different access layers.','A regulated service uses an NLB TCP listener and web servers integrated with a multi-AZ CloudHSM cluster for private-key operations.','Who manages cryptographic users in CloudHSM?','You manage HSM users and keys; AWS manages the underlying hardware service.')
L(2,127,134,'S3 security, signed access & WORM','S3 authorization, encryption, network path, dan retention adalah empat lapisan yang berbeda.','SSE-S3 uses S3-managed keys; SSE-KMS adds KMS control/audit; SSE-C supplies customer keys with requests; client-side encryption happens before upload.~Bucket policies, IAM policies, Block Public Access and Object Ownership govern access. A presigned URL delegates a specific signed operation and expires no later than its signing credentials.~Object Lock protects object versions. Governance mode can be bypassed with authorized permissions; compliance retention cannot be shortened during its protected period. Legal holds are separate.','Use presigned uploads to let clients send large objects directly to S3. Use compliance retention for strict immutable records.','Presigned URL is a bearer capability, not a new IAM identity. Default encryption does not by itself deny uploads using an unwanted encryption choice.','An authenticated app issues a short-lived PUT URL for one exact object key; the client uploads directly instead of passing a large file through API Gateway.','Does a bucket-level permission use the same ARN as an object-level permission?','No. ListBucket targets the bucket ARN; GetObject/PutObject target object ARNs such as bucket/prefix/*.')
L(2,135,140,'S3 access points & multi-Region access','Access point = pintu bernama dengan policy tersendiri untuk dataset yang sama.','Use access points to separate team access by prefix or application. A VPC-only access point also needs an appropriate VPC endpoint and policies.~Multi-Region Access Points route through a global endpoint to regional buckets. Replication and failover controls are separate decisions; do not assume routing copies the data.~S3 Object Lambda transforms content during retrieval in the slide architecture. Its availability for new customers has changed; keep the pattern distinct from a new deployment recommendation.','Many teams sharing one bucket: access points. Global bucket routing with controlled failover: MRAP plus designed replication.','“Nearest bucket” is useful only if the required object exists there. Asynchronous replication permits lag.','Finance gets a /finance access point; analytics gets read-only access. Both use the same bucket while retaining different policies.','If MRAP is created, are all historical objects automatically replicated?','No. Configure replication and address existing objects separately, for example with supported batch replication.')
L(2,141,156,'WAF, Shield & Firewall Manager','WAF memeriksa HTTP requests; Shield menghadapi DDoS; Firewall Manager menyebarkan policies secara terpusat.','Shield Standard provides baseline protection; Advanced adds supported enhanced protections and response capabilities. WAF handles L7 rules, managed rule groups, IP sets and rate-based controls.~CloudFront and Route 53 distribute exposure at the edge. Protect origins too: VPC origins or restricted network access plus appropriately protected origin headers where applicable.~Use Firewall Manager for consistent supported security policies across organization accounts.','SQL injection or HTTP abuse: WAF. Large DDoS requirements: Shield strategy. Consistency across accounts: Firewall Manager.','WAF can help mitigate application-layer DDoS; “WAF is not for DDoS” is too absolute. An ALB’s client-facing HTTP identity differs from the network peer seen behind CloudFront.','Block a malicious viewer IP at WAF on CloudFront. Blocking a CloudFront edge IP at the origin could block many legitimate users.','Does a security group have a deny rule?','No. SGs allow traffic. Use the appropriate NACL, WAF or firewall for explicit blocking at the relevant layer.')
L(2,157,165,'Inspector, Config & GuardDuty','Vulnerability, compliance, dan threat detection bukan hal yang sama.','Inspector finds supported workload vulnerabilities, including relevant EC2, container and Lambda findings.~Config records resource configuration and evaluates compliance. Rules can invoke remediation using Systems Manager; configuration recording alone does not prevent a change.~GuardDuty analyzes supported telemetry for suspicious activity. Delegated administration supports organization-wide management; findings can trigger EventBridge response workflows.','Known vulnerable package: Inspector. Public security group violates policy: Config. Compromised instance behavior: GuardDuty.','A detective finding is evidence to investigate, not proof that automated destructive remediation is always appropriate. Do not confuse a Config aggregator with a recorder in every account.','An instance contacting a suspicious destination triggers GuardDuty; its vulnerable package appears in Inspector; its open SSH rule appears in Config.','Which service answers “how did this security group change over time”?','AWS Config for configuration history, with CloudTrail to identify the API caller.')
L(2,166,173,'Security investigation & access context','Conditions mempersempit izin berdasarkan konteks. Security Hub mengumpulkan findings; Detective membantu investigasi.','Use aws:PrincipalOrgID in a resource policy to constrain access to organization members, alongside required permissions.~SourceIp, SourceVpc and SourceVpce describe different paths. For endpoint requests, use the correct context keys rather than assuming the public-source-IP key applies.~EC2 Instance Connect pushes short-lived SSH keys but still requires SSH connectivity for that connection mode. Security Hub centralizes findings; Detective builds investigation context.','Need shell access without opening inbound SSH: Session Manager. Need correlated findings: Security Hub. Need root-cause context: Detective.','CloudTrail logging StartSession is not the same as recording every command. SSH/port-forwarded Session Manager traffic has session-content logging limitations.','A resource policy trusts only the organization, while a separate IAM role limits which objects the responder may inspect.','Security Hub or Detective for aggregating security findings?','Security Hub aggregates and prioritizes findings. Detective helps investigate relationships and suspicious activity.')
L(3,174,190,'EC2, placement & high-performance computing','Pilih compute dari bottleneck: CPU, RAM, I/O, GPU, atau komunikasi antar-node.','General-purpose, compute, memory, storage and accelerated families serve different workload shapes. Graviton requires compatible Arm software.~Cluster placement favors low-latency communication in one AZ. Spread reduces correlated hardware failure; partition placement separates groups of racks for distributed systems.~ENA improves networking; EFA supports tightly coupled HPC. Pair appropriate compute with FSx for Lustre, EBS or local scratch, and use Batch/ParallelCluster for orchestration.','Low-latency MPI job: cluster placement plus supported EFA instances. Rack-aware distributed data: partition placement. Independent critical nodes: spread.','A cluster placement group optimizes locality, not multi-AZ availability. RAM is not a default EC2 CloudWatch metric; install an agent.','A simulation uses EFA nodes and Lustre for parallel input while durable results go to S3. Local scratch can be lost and regenerated.','Which placement group deliberately separates rack partitions?','Partition placement. The application can use partition information to distribute replicas.')
L(3,191,200,'Auto Scaling: match demand without instability','Scaling menambah capacity; health replacement mengganti resource rusak. Dua mekanisme berbeda.','Target tracking maintains a utilization target; step policies respond to alarm bands; scheduled scaling anticipates known peaks; predictive scaling forecasts patterns.~Lifecycle hooks pause launch/termination for preparation or cleanup. Instance Refresh replaces instances using a new launch-template version while respecting health/warm-up settings.~Use an application-relevant metric: queue backlog per worker, requests per target, CPU or another real bottleneck. Health checks should identify unhealthy instances without triggering mass replacement because a shared dependency fails.','Select the scaling signal that tracks per-instance demand and allow realistic warm-up time.','Changing an AMI in a template does not modify existing instances. A database outage should not cause every healthy web server to be endlessly replaced.','At 120 requests/s and a target of 30 per instance, approximately four ready instances are needed, subject to headroom and workload behavior.','What does Instance Refresh solve?','It rolls existing ASG instances onto a new template/configuration; editing the template alone affects future launches.')
L(3,201,203,'Spot & purchase models','Spot = capacity murah yang boleh diambil kembali. Desain harus tahan interruption.','Use checkpointing, retryable tasks and diversified instance types/AZs. Price-capacity-optimized allocation balances available capacity and price.~On-Demand handles flexible reliable baseline needs. Savings Plans and RIs exchange commitment for billing discounts. Dedicated Hosts offer physical host control useful for certain licenses.~A mixed ASG or fleet can maintain an On-Demand baseline while using Spot for expendable workers.','Fault-tolerant batch or stateless workers: consider Spot. Non-interruptible stateful singleton: do not rely solely on Spot.','Spot interruption can result from capacity needs, not just price. A billing discount is not always a capacity reservation.','Video chunks are independent, checkpointed and queued; interrupted workers are replaced and unacknowledged chunks retry.','Does Reserved Instance mean a special VM image?','No. It is primarily a purchasing/billing construct, with capacity-reservation behavior depending on the reservation scope.')
L(3,204,216,'ECS, Fargate & ECR','ECR menyimpan image; ECS menjadwalkan tasks; Fargate menjalankan containers tanpa kamu mengelola EC2 hosts.','Task definition describes containers, resources and networking. A task is a running copy; a service maintains the desired task count.~Separate the task role (application AWS API access), task execution role (platform actions such as pulling images/secrets), and EC2 instance role where used.~awsvpc gives tasks their own networking/SGs. Bridge-mode EC2 tasks can use dynamic port mapping. Scale services and underlying EC2 capacity appropriately; Fargate removes host-capacity management.','Minimum container-host operations: ECS on Fargate. Need host control or specialized EC2 options: ECS on EC2.','Image scanning finds vulnerabilities; it does not patch the image. A rotated injected secret requires a refresh strategy. Task scaling alone does not add EC2 host capacity.','A task writes invoices to S3 using its task role; its execution role lets ECS pull the image from ECR and inject the startup secret.','Which role grants application code access to DynamoDB?','The ECS task role, scoped to the table and required actions.')
L(3,217,222,'EKS & containers outside AWS','EKS memakai Kubernetes APIs; ECS memakai AWS-native orchestration. Pilih berdasarkan kebutuhan platform yang nyata.','EKS manages the Kubernetes control plane. Managed node groups simplify EC2 node management; self-managed nodes give more control; Fargate fits supported pod workloads.~Storage uses CSI drivers and compatible StorageClasses. An EBS volume is AZ-bound; EFS provides shared NFS access across AZs where supported.~ECS Anywhere extends AWS-managed ECS scheduling to external infrastructure with agents. EKS Anywhere runs Kubernetes on customer-managed infrastructure with its own operational model.','Existing Kubernetes skills, manifests and ecosystem requirements favor EKS. A simple container requirement alone does not require Kubernetes.','Container images are not automatically portable across every OS/CPU. A managed control plane does not eliminate application, pod, node or network responsibilities.','A company moves existing Kubernetes workloads to EKS, checks CSI and networking compatibility, and retains Kubernetes deployment workflows.','Is ECS Anywhere the same as EKS Anywhere?','No. ECS Anywhere extends ECS control to external hosts; EKS Anywhere is Kubernetes deployed outside AWS with a different control/operations model.')
L(3,223,236,'Lambda: invocation, concurrency & networking','Lambda menjalankan functions saat ada trigger. Concurrency adalah jumlah executions yang berjalan bersamaan.','Synchronous callers receive the result and handle invocation retries. Asynchronous invocation queues events and has retry/destination controls. SQS uses event-source polling with queue semantics.~Reserved concurrency caps and reserves function concurrency; provisioned concurrency keeps environments prepared to reduce startup latency.~VPC-attached Lambda can reach private databases. Internet egress needs a working route through NAT; placing it in a public subnet does not give it a public IP.','Short event-driven work: Lambda. Use SQS and controlled concurrency to protect a slow downstream service.','One standard invocation is limited to 15 minutes. At 1,769 MB the CPU equivalent is one vCPU. Lambda concurrency is not requests per second.','100 requests/s × 0.2 seconds average duration ≈ 20 concurrent executions. NAT with an EIP gives external APIs a fixed outbound IP.','How can a Lambda call a private RDS instance and a public API?','Attach it to appropriate private subnets/SGs; use private connectivity to RDS and a NAT route for the public API.')
L(3,237,252,'ALB, NLB & GWLB','ALB memahami HTTP; NLB mengarahkan network flows; GWLB memasukkan security appliances ke jalur traffic.','ALB supports host/path/header routing and targets such as instances, IPs and Lambda. NLB serves supported TCP/UDP/TLS workloads with static zonal addresses.~GWLB distributes encapsulated traffic to inspection appliances using GENEVE. Route design must steer traffic through the inspection path.~Cross-zone balancing spreads traffic across AZ targets. Stickiness may preserve affinity but cause imbalance; external session storage supports stateless application tiers.','HTTP path routing: ALB. Static IP plus TCP/UDP: NLB. Third-party transparent inspection fleet: GWLB.','ALB supports mutual TLS. Cross-zone can be disabled at supported ALB target groups, so the slide’s “always on, cannot disable” is incomplete.','Two AZs contain 2 and 8 targets. With equal zonal ingress, disabling cross-zone produces much more traffic per target in the smaller AZ.','Does NLB use HTTP path rules?','No. If static IPs and ALB HTTP routing are both needed, a supported NLB-to-ALB architecture can combine them.')
L(3,253,263,'API Gateway: management, security & limits','API Gateway adalah front door API dengan authentication, throttling, stages dan integrations.','Use direct AWS service integration when no custom Lambda logic is needed. Stages separate deployed versions; caching and usage plans are API-type-specific features.~IAM SigV4, Cognito/JWT and Lambda authorizers solve authentication/authorization. API keys meter usage; they are not strong authentication. CORS is a browser-enforced cross-origin permission mechanism.~Diagnose 4xx/5xx with gateway and integration metrics/logs. A 502 alone does not prove a concurrency problem.','Large uploads: generate a presigned S3 URL. Public API with auth/throttling: API Gateway. Simple mixed HTTP targets: ALB may suffice.','The 29-second integration timeout is not universal: some Regional/private REST APIs support quota increases. Distinguish REST, HTTP and WebSocket API features.','A 100 MB upload bypasses the gateway payload ceiling by going from client directly to S3 after an authorized URL request.','Why is enabling CORS on S3 insufficient for a browser calling an API?','The API response must permit the web page’s origin; configure CORS on the API endpoint being called.')
L(3,264,269,'WebSockets & AppSync GraphQL','WebSocket mempertahankan koneksi dua arah. GraphQL menentukan data yang diminta dan resolvers yang mengambilnya.','API Gateway WebSockets manage connection events and route messages. Store connection IDs if the backend needs to send messages through the connection-management API.~AppSync resolves GraphQL fields against supported data sources or Lambda and supports real-time application patterns.~Authentication to Cognito is separate from resolver IAM permission to read the backing data source.','Real-time bidirectional messaging with custom routes: WebSocket API. Unified GraphQL access to multiple data sources: AppSync.','An authenticated user must still be authorized for a particular operation or record. GraphQL does not remove the need to design access control.','A delivery dashboard subscribes to order-status updates while a resolver reads order details from DynamoDB.','Does AppSync replace DynamoDB?','No. It is an API layer that uses data sources such as DynamoDB, Aurora, HTTP endpoints or Lambda.')
L(3,270,285,'Route 53: records & routing choices','DNS menjawab alamat tujuan. Setelah jawaban di-cache, client mungkin belum melihat perubahan berikutnya.','A/AAAA map to IPv4/IPv6. CNAME aliases another hostname but not the zone apex. Route 53 Alias supports selected targets and apex records.~Weighted routing distributes DNS answers by weights; latency chooses measured regional latency; geolocation uses user geography; geoproximity includes bias; IP-based routing uses CIDR mappings.~Failover chooses primary/secondary health-based records. Multivalue returns several healthy answers; it is not a replacement for a load balancer.','Canary by DNS: weighted. Lowest regional latency: latency. Country-specific answer: geolocation. Simple active/passive recovery: failover.','Weighted DNS is not an exact percentage of HTTP requests because resolvers and clients cache responses. Lower TTL speeds change visibility but increases DNS queries.','A resolver caches a blue-environment address for 300 seconds; a DNS swap does not immediately move every existing client.','Can an Alias point directly at an arbitrary EC2 public DNS name?','No. Alias supports specific target types; use an appropriate A record or other valid DNS design.')
L(3,286,293,'DNS health, hosted zones & failover','Public hosted zone untuk internet DNS; private hosted zone untuk associated VPCs. Health check menentukan availability signal.','Public health checkers cannot directly reach private-only endpoints. Publish a suitable CloudWatch metric/alarm and use an alarm-based health check for private resources.~Calculated checks combine health signals. Ensure health checks represent service readiness and allow checker traffic where required.~DNSSEC authenticates DNS data. Private hosted zone resolution requires appropriate VPC DNS settings and associations.','Private database failover signal: custom metric/alarm plus controlled promotion and DNS updates.','Changing DNS does not promote a read replica, synchronize lost writes or repair application connection pools. Those are separate recovery steps.','An automated runbook verifies primary failure, promotes the replica, changes the application endpoint and validates writes in the recovery region.','Can Route 53 endpoint health checks reach 10.0.1.10 directly?','No. Use a reachable health endpoint or an alarm-based signal derived from inside the private environment.')
L(3,294,298,'Hybrid DNS: inbound vs outbound Resolver','Arah endpoint dilihat dari sisi AWS: inbound = masuk AWS, outbound = keluar AWS menuju DNS kamu.','Inbound endpoints let on-premises resolvers query AWS private DNS. Outbound endpoints send matching VPC DNS queries to on-premises DNS servers.~Forwarding rules define domains and target DNS servers; more specific matching rules win. System rules can override forwarding for selected namespaces.~Deploy endpoint IPs across AZs, permit DNS traffic, provide VPN/DX routing and share Resolver rules with RAM where appropriate.','On-premises asks for an AWS private name: inbound. EC2 asks for an internal corporate name: outbound.','A network connection alone does not create conditional DNS forwarding. Do not forward every domain both ways and accidentally create a loop.','EC2 asks payroll.corp.internal; the outbound rule forwards only corp.internal to the corporate DNS over a private network path.','What is shared centrally to reuse outbound forwarding across accounts?','Supported Route 53 Resolver rules through AWS RAM, associated with the consuming VPCs.')
L(3,299,312,'Global entry points & architecture selection','Tentukan apakah masalahnya caching, global routing, DNS, atau compute scaling.','CloudFront caches content and accelerates HTTP delivery. Global Accelerator routes supported TCP/UDP traffic over AWS’s network using stable anycast addresses and endpoint health.~An EIP on one instance provides a fixed address but is not a scalable multi-AZ architecture. ALB+ASG adds health routing and horizontal capacity; containers or Lambda alter the compute operating model.~API Gateway direct integration removes unnecessary Lambda code for supported service-proxy tasks.','Static global addresses or non-HTTP acceleration: Global Accelerator. Cacheable HTTP content: CloudFront. API policies: API Gateway.','Global Accelerator does not cache objects. CloudFront is not merely static-only. Neither removes database failover or downstream-capacity constraints.','A UDP game uses Global Accelerator; its web assets use CloudFront/S3; purchase APIs use API Gateway with appropriate authentication.','Why put API Gateway directly in front of SQS?','When the request only needs authorized message submission, direct integration avoids an unnecessary Lambda hop and its operations/cost.')
L(3,313,317,'Outposts, Local Zones & Wavelength','AWS Region diperluas ke lokasi yang berbeda untuk alasan latency atau data placement.','Outposts puts selected AWS infrastructure/services in customer premises, with physical-site responsibilities and a regional service connection.~Local Zones put selected AWS services nearer metropolitan users while remaining associated with a parent Region.~Wavelength places supported infrastructure within telecom networks for suitable low-latency applications. Service and location availability vary.','Data must stay in your own facility: consider Outposts. Metro proximity: Local Zones. Telecom-edge use case: Wavelength.','“AWS-like experience on premises” does not make every AWS service available locally or every workload disconnected-capable.','A factory processes latency-sensitive data on Outposts and sends permitted aggregated results to its parent Region.','Which option is installed in a customer’s data center?','AWS Outposts.')
# Additional chapters appended below.
L(4,318,327,'EBS, snapshots & instance store','Block storage terlihat seperti disk. EBS persistent melalui network; instance store menempel pada host dan bersifat ephemeral.','Choose gp3 for typical general-purpose SSD workloads; provisioned-IOPS SSD for demanding latency/IOPS; throughput HDD for suitable sequential workloads, not boot disks.~EBS is AZ-scoped. Snapshots are incremental backups used to restore volumes, copy across Regions and create AMIs. Quiesce application writes for consistency; Fast Snapshot Restore avoids initialization latency where configured.~Multi-Attach supports certain io1/io2 uses in one AZ and needs application/filesystem coordination. Instance store survives reboot, but not stop/termination or underlying disk loss.','Persistent VM disk: EBS. Re-creatable ultra-fast scratch: instance store. Shared file semantics across AZs: EFS/appropriate FSx.','Multi-Attach does not turn ordinary ext4/XFS into a safe multi-writer cluster filesystem. Increasing volume size may also require filesystem expansion.','A database uses durable EBS; an analytics worker uses local scratch and writes completed results to S3 before termination.','Why can a restored EBS volume initially feel slower?','Blocks may be initialized lazily from the snapshot. Use suitable pre-initialization or Fast Snapshot Restore when needed.')
L(4,328,335,'EFS: shared Linux files','EFS = shared NFS filesystem untuk banyak clients. Access point dapat memberi setiap aplikasi directory dan POSIX identity tersendiri.','Regional EFS supports multi-AZ access via mount targets; One Zone trades AZ resilience for cost. Security groups, IAM/file-system policies and POSIX permissions all matter.~Choose throughput mode for workload behavior: bursting, provisioned or elastic where supported. Lifecycle policies can move cold files into cheaper classes with different access costs.~EFS replication supports recovery copies; plan destination promotion, network access and actual recovery testing.','Shared Linux web content or application files: EFS. Windows SMB/NTFS requirement: FSx for Windows.','Throughput, IOPS and capacity are different dimensions. A read/write IAM allow cannot automatically override all filesystem permission constraints.','Several web servers in different AZs mount EFS; separate app access points restrict each app to its own root directory.','What does an EFS access point enforce?','An application-specific path and optional POSIX user/group identity, combined with relevant IAM and network controls.')
L(4,336,340,'S3 objects, lifecycle & replication','S3 menyimpan objects dengan keys, bukan block disk atau POSIX shared drive.','Select a storage class from access frequency, retrieval delay, AZ resilience and minimum storage charges. Lifecycle transitions move data by rules.~CRR and SRR copy eligible objects between versioned buckets. Replication is asynchronous; existing objects and deletion behavior require deliberate configuration. RTC provides a specified replication-time service commitment for eligible objects.~Native S3 events can go to supported destinations or EventBridge for richer routing. Consumers must handle retries/duplicates.','Static assets and durable object datasets: S3. Multi-Region recovery: replication plus failover/readiness planning.','S3 strong read-after-write consistency does not imply synchronous cross-Region replication. A replica bucket is not inherently read-only.','A photo upload emits an event, Lambda creates a thumbnail, and a separate replication rule copies eligible originals for DR.','Does lifecycle automatically create a second regional copy?','No. Lifecycle changes storage/retention within its scope; replication creates another copy.')
L(4,341,354,'S3 performance, analytics & metadata indexes','Optimalkan transfer, request distribution, dan data organization sebelum menambah compute.','Multipart upload parallelizes large uploads; byte-range GET parallelizes downloads or reads only a portion. Abort incomplete multipart uploads with lifecycle rules to avoid paying for abandoned parts.~Spread request load across prefixes where useful and consider KMS request capacity with SSE-KMS. Transfer Acceleration uses the edge network for suitable long-distance transfers.~Storage Class Analysis informs lifecycle choices; Storage Lens aggregates storage/activity/protection insights. A DynamoDB metadata index supports custom access patterns over uploaded objects.','Need search by customer/date over object metadata: maintain an index. Need organization-wide storage visibility: Storage Lens.','A filename extension filter in events is a prefix/suffix match, not an arbitrary wildcard engine. Extra prefixes do not solve a single hot object by themselves.','Store immutable product images in S3, metadata in DynamoDB, and deliver images through CloudFront. Query the index rather than listing every object.','Why delete incomplete multipart parts?','They consume billable storage even though the upload never became a completed object.')
L(4,355,363,'Choose the correct FSx filesystem','Nama protocol sering langsung menentukan jawaban: SMB, NFS, iSCSI, atau Lustre.','FSx for Windows supports SMB, NTFS/AD integration and Windows share semantics. FSx for Lustre serves parallel HPC/ML workloads and integrates with S3 datasets.~Lustre scratch is temporary; persistent deployments replicate within their deployment design. Lazy loading fetches data as needed instead of waiting for an entire dataset.~FSx for NetApp ONTAP supports NFS, SMB and iSCSI with ONTAP capabilities. OpenZFS fits NFS/ZFS workloads. Migration and resizing constraints differ by filesystem.','Windows file shares: FSx Windows. Parallel analytics over S3: Lustre. Existing ONTAP/multiprotocol: ONTAP. ZFS/NFS semantics: OpenZFS.','Do not apply one FSx product’s storage-resizing rules to every FSx product. For Windows downsizing, create a smaller target and migrate data.','A team needs AD-integrated SMB shares across AZs: select FSx Windows Multi-AZ rather than EFS or S3 alone.','Why use Lustre with S3 for an HPC job?','It provides a high-performance parallel filesystem while S3 remains a durable dataset repository.')
L(4,364,374,'DataSync, Transfer Family & Data Exchange','DataSync memindahkan data; Transfer Family melayani file-transfer clients; Data Exchange menyediakan data pihak ketiga.','DataSync transfers supported file/object data between locations with verification, scheduling and supported metadata preservation. Agent requirements depend on source/destination type.~Transfer Family exposes supported SFTP/FTPS/FTP interfaces backed by supported S3/EFS configurations. Endpoint type determines private/public access and network controls.~Data Exchange is for subscribing to third-party datasets or supported data products. Compare total storage cost including operations, retrieval and transfer, not only GB-month.','One-time or recurring migration/synchronization: DataSync. Partners insist on SFTP: Transfer Family. Purchased external dataset: Data Exchange.','SFTP and FTPS are different protocols. Moving data into S3 does not preserve every filesystem behavior for applications.','A supplier keeps its SFTP client while Transfer Family writes files into S3; an EventBridge-triggered pipeline processes arrivals.','Why not use Transfer Family for a large NFS migration by default?','DataSync directly targets that transfer/synchronization job with supported verification and metadata handling; Transfer Family targets protocol-based client access.')
L(5,375,387,'CloudFront origins, failover & price classes','CDN cache menaruh response dekat pengguna sehingga origin menerima lebih sedikit requests.','Use OAC to protect supported S3 origins. S3 website endpoints behave as custom origins and differ from private S3 REST origins. VPC origins support eligible private application origins.~Origin groups provide failover for supported methods/conditions. Cache behaviors and TTLs determine which content is cached and how long.~Price classes trade edge-location coverage for cost; geo restrictions control viewer countries, not legal proof of user residency.','Global web assets: CloudFront/S3. Reduce database load only when the relevant response can be safely cached.','Origin failover is not a general replay-safe failover for every POST/write. Protect origins against bypassing the CDN.','A product image uses a long TTL and versioned filename. Personalized account data needs an appropriate private/no-cache policy and authorization.','Is CloudFront replication the same as S3 CRR?','No. A cache can evict data and follows TTLs; replication creates a separate durable bucket copy.')
L(5,388,390,'Signed URLs, signed cookies & errors','Signed access memberi izin sementara tanpa menjadikan seluruh content publik.','CloudFront signed URLs/cookies are created by an authorized application using a private signing key; trusted key groups are the recommended signer-management approach.~A signed URL usually authorizes a selected resource; signed cookies help when many protected files must be accessed without changing each URL.~S3 presigned URLs instead sign S3 operations using IAM credentials. Custom error pages and error caching need suitable TTLs to avoid prolonging a recovered error.','Protected video files delivered by CDN: CloudFront signed access. Direct object PUT/GET: S3 presigned URL.','CloudFront signing does not require a root-managed account key pair when using trusted key groups. Signing is done by your application; not every URL requires a CloudFront API call.','A paid video player receives signed cookies covering its protected streaming files while the S3 origin remains private via OAC.','Why might users keep seeing an error after the origin recovers?','CloudFront may still cache the error response according to its error caching settings.')
L(5,391,402,'CloudFront Functions vs Lambda@Edge','Pilih tempat eksekusi berdasarkan event, kebutuhan network, dan kompleksitas logic.','CloudFront Functions handles lightweight JavaScript at viewer request/response events: normalization, redirects, simple validation and headers.~Lambda@Edge supports viewer and origin events with richer execution capabilities and supported network access. Deploy its source function in us-east-1 as required.~Viewer-request logic runs before cache lookup; origin-request logic runs when an origin fetch is needed. Cache-key design determines whether user-specific responses can be safely reused.','Simple URL/header normalization: CloudFront Functions. Origin selection or logic requiring supported external calls: Lambda@Edge.','Do not cache personalized content under a key shared by all users. CloudFront Functions and Lambda@Edge cannot both handle viewer events on the same behavior in the incompatible combination.','Normalize tracking query parameters out of the cache key so equivalent public image requests reuse one cached object.','Which event avoids running on every cache hit when only origin routing must change?','An origin-request Lambda@Edge event, because it runs on requests that proceed to the origin.')
L(5,403,407,'ElastiCache & stateless applications','Cache adalah salinan cepat yang boleh stale. Session store menyimpan state bersama agar app servers bisa diganti.','Cache-aside: check cache, read database on a miss, then populate cache. Use TTL and invalidation to manage stale data; choose a policy for cache outages.~Redis/Valkey-style capabilities include rich structures and replication options. Memcached fits simpler caching; supported durability features depend on deployment type.~Move sessions out of individual EC2 instances so any healthy instance can serve the next request. Cache is not a replacement for durable business records.','General application/session cache: ElastiCache. DynamoDB-compatible read acceleration: DAX.','A cache improves read latency but does not repair a poorly designed write path. Sticky sessions alone do not make session data resilient to instance loss.','If 80% of 1,000 requests/s hit cache, roughly 200 requests/s reach the origin under a simple independent-request model.','What must you design before introducing cache?','Keys, TTL/invalidation, acceptable staleness, miss handling and behavior when the cache is unavailable.')
L(6,408,418,'DynamoDB: keys, indexes, streams & DAX','Desain DynamoDB dimulai dari access patterns. Partition key menyebarkan data; sort key mengurutkan items dalam partition.','Primary keys may be partition-only or partition-plus-sort. Query uses key conditions; Scan reads broadly. LSI keeps the partition key and is created with the table; GSI supplies another key path and can be added later.~Choose on-demand or provisioned capacity. Item size is limited; transactions and consistent reads consume different capacity from basic eventual reads.~TTL removes expired items asynchronously. Streams expose changes; global tables replicate across Regions. DAX accelerates compatible reads, not writes or strongly consistent reads from cache.','Predictable key-value access at scale: DynamoDB. Frequent alternative lookup: appropriate GSI. Repeated eventually consistent reads: DAX.','A hot partition key can throttle even if total table capacity looks adequate. DAX does require client configuration and is not a fix for hot writes.','Orders use customerId as partition key and orderTimestamp as sort key; a GSI supports a separate lookup by order status if distribution is safe.','Can you add an LSI after table creation?','No. Plan LSIs at table creation; GSIs can be added later.')
L(6,419,422,'OpenSearch: search and log analytics','Search engine membangun index untuk full-text search dan analytics; biasanya bukan source of truth transaksi.','OpenSearch indexes documents and supports search/aggregation. Dashboards visualizes indexed data; ingestion pipelines move and transform source events.~A DynamoDB Stream plus consumer can maintain a searchable copy. CloudWatch subscriptions and supported ingestion paths supply logs.~Decide freshness, retries, replay, index mappings, retention and recovery from missed updates.','Need text search/flexible document search over operational data: OpenSearch. Need primary keyed writes: DynamoDB or an appropriate transactional database.','Adding a search index creates another copy that can lag. Do not promise immediate transactional consistency across database and search index.','The application writes an order to DynamoDB, and a stream consumer indexes it for customer-service search.','Which system should be authoritative for an order payment?','The designed transactional system of record, not a potentially lagging search index.')
L(6,423,431,'RDS: availability, replicas & connection pooling','Multi-AZ untuk availability; read replica untuk read scaling. Lihat jenis deployment sebelum menyimpulkan behavior.','RDS manages supported database infrastructure, backups and maintenance. Automated backups support PITR; manual snapshots have their own retention lifecycle.~Traditional Multi-AZ DB instances use a non-readable standby; read replicas asynchronously serve reads and can support DR. Multi-AZ DB clusters have a different readable-standby model.~RDS Proxy pools connections, especially valuable for bursty Lambda workloads. IAM DB authentication establishes supported database login; SQL authorization remains inside the database.','Write availability in one Region: appropriate Multi-AZ deployment. Read bottleneck: replicas. Connection storms: RDS Proxy.','Read replicas do not automatically fix write saturation. Cross-Region promotion is a recovery workflow. RDS for Oracle does not provide every self-managed Oracle feature, such as RAC.','Thousands of Lambda executions share a smaller connection pool through RDS Proxy instead of opening a separate long-lived backend connection each.','Does CloudTrail show every SELECT statement?','No. Use appropriate database logs/auditing and performance tools for SQL-level investigation.')
L(6,432,438,'Aurora: shared storage & endpoints','Aurora memisahkan compute instances dari distributed storage. Endpoints mengarahkan koneksi berdasarkan peran.','The writer/cluster endpoint targets the current writer. The reader endpoint balances connections among eligible replicas; custom endpoints target chosen subsets. Instance endpoints target a specific instance.~Aurora storage maintains multiple copies across AZs and supports replica failover. Reader scaling and writer capacity remain separate concerns.~Use database metrics, supported performance tools and slow-query logs to diagnose CPU, waits, connections or query issues before selecting a scaling action.','Separate heavy analytics onto suitable replicas/custom endpoints. Use the writer endpoint for writes and recovery-aware connection handling.','Reader endpoints balance connections, not each SQL statement. Long-lived connections may distribute unevenly. An endpoint does not enforce all SQL permissions.','A custom endpoint routes report connections to larger replicas while ordinary application reads use another eligible group.','Will adding readers necessarily accelerate slow writes?','No. Diagnose the writer bottleneck; replicas primarily provide read capacity and failover options.')
L(6,439,444,'Aurora Serverless, Global Database & migration','Serverless capacity scaling dan cross-Region disaster recovery adalah keputusan terpisah.','Aurora Serverless adapts supported compute capacity to demand; configure its bounds and check engine/version support. Data API exposes supported SQL access through HTTPS; availability is not limited to one historical Aurora mode.~Global Database uses a primary writer Region and secondary Regions for low-latency reads and DR. Write forwarding sends writes to the primary; it is not independent multi-writer conflict resolution.~Migration from supported RDS engines can use snapshots or a replica/promotion path as applicable.','Variable relational workload: evaluate Serverless. Regional recovery and global reads: evaluate Global Database.','Do not treat illustrative replication lag or failover time as guaranteed RPO/RTO. Test end-to-end recovery including application reconnection.','Singapore readers query a secondary; a write is forwarded to the primary and replicated back, so cross-Region write latency still exists.','Does write forwarding make a secondary an independent writer?','No. The authoritative write still happens in the primary Region.')
L(7,445,455,'Step Functions: orchestration & error handling','State machine menjelaskan urutan, cabang, paralelisme, retry, wait, dan hasil setiap langkah.','Use optimized/service SDK integrations to orchestrate work without unnecessary glue functions. Long-running jobs can use supported wait-for-completion patterns; human approvals can use callback tokens.~Standard workflows support long duration and detailed execution history. Express targets short high-volume workflows; synchronous and asynchronous Express have different execution semantics.~Set Retry with backoff, Catch for recovery, and timeouts. Alert on failed execution with EventBridge.','Human approval or long orchestration: Standard. High-volume short idempotent event processing: consider Express.','“Exactly once workflow execution” does not make every external side effect exactly once if a task is retried. Design task idempotency.','A workflow validates an order, charges payment with an idempotency key, waits for fulfillment and records failure compensation where needed.','Why not keep a Lambda running while waiting for approval?','Lambda has an invocation time limit and consumes execution resources. A state-machine wait/callback is designed for that pause.')
L(7,456,461,'SQS: visibility, retries & idempotency','Queue menyerap lonjakan. Receive menyembunyikan message sementara; Delete mengakui bahwa pekerjaan selesai.','Standard queues provide at-least-once delivery and best-effort ordering. Visibility timeout hides a received message while processing. If it is not deleted in time, it becomes available again.~Use long polling to reduce empty responses. A DLQ isolates repeatedly failing messages; inspect/fix before redrive. Match queue types as required.~For Lambda, event-source mapping polls the queue. Configure batch failure handling, visibility timeout and concurrency to avoid unnecessary retries and overload.','Decouple a slow service with SQS and rate/concurrency-controlled workers. Use an idempotency key for payments or other side effects.','An upsert is not automatically idempotent: an increment executed twice still doubles its effect. FIFO does not eliminate the need for safe retry handling.','Order 123 is retried after a timeout. A conditional record/check on its processing ID prevents a second charge.','Where does the poison-message DLQ belong for SQS-triggered Lambda?','On the source SQS queue via its redrive policy, rather than relying on Lambda’s asynchronous invocation DLQ.')
L(7,462,463,'Amazon MQ: protocol compatibility','MQ = managed broker untuk aplikasi yang bergantung pada broker protocols dan semantics.','Existing applications may rely on ActiveMQ/RabbitMQ-compatible protocols and messaging behavior such as AMQP, MQTT, STOMP or OpenWire, depending on engine.~Amazon MQ reduces broker infrastructure operations but requires engine compatibility, capacity planning and suitable HA configuration.~SQS/SNS provide highly managed cloud-native APIs and scaling, but migrating to them can require application changes.','Minimum changes for a supported legacy broker workload: Amazon MQ. New cloud-native decoupling without protocol constraints: consider SQS/SNS.','A managed broker is not automatically a drop-in replacement for every proprietary broker feature. Validate the required protocol and semantics.','A legacy application uses a supported ActiveMQ client and moves to a Multi-AZ Amazon MQ deployment after compatibility testing.','Why might SQS be the wrong migration answer even though it scales well?','The application may require an existing broker protocol/behavior and the question may demand minimal code changes.')
L(7,464,477,'SNS fan-out, filtering & delivery failures','SNS menyebarkan satu message ke banyak subscribers. SQS menyimpan pekerjaan sampai worker memprosesnya.','Attach a queue per independent consumer to an SNS topic. Each consumer can retry and scale independently; queue policies must allow the topic to send.~Subscription filters select relevant events. FIFO topic/queue designs provide ordering within message groups and deduplication behavior, subject to supported subscription types.~SNS delivery retries depend on endpoint type. A subscription DLQ records exhausted delivery attempts; it is distinct from the worker queue’s processing DLQ.','One order needs independent fraud/shipping/accounting processing: SNS → separate SQS queues.','Multiple workers on one SQS queue compete for messages; they do not each get every message. SNS without a queue is not the same durable work-buffer design.','Fraud delays for ten minutes while shipping continues from its own queue. Shipping does not wait for the fraud queue to drain.','Where is an SNS delivery DLQ attached?','To a subscription. It handles delivery failures to that subscriber, not every application-processing failure after delivery.')
L(8,478,490,'Streaming: Kinesis, Firehose & Flink','Stream menyimpan ordered event log untuk dibaca ulang; delivery service mengirim data ke destination; processor menghitung di atas stream.','Kinesis Data Streams provides replay and independent consumers, ordered within shards for a key. Provisioned shards have write-byte, write-record and read-capacity limits; hot keys can dominate one shard.~Amazon Data Firehose buffers and delivers to supported destinations, with optional transformations and format conversion. It is not a consumer replay store.~Managed Service for Apache Flink performs stateful stream computations such as event-time windows and aggregations over supported sources.','Replay/multiple real-time consumers: Kinesis. Managed delivery into S3: Firehose. Stateful streaming analytics: Flink.','A partition key hashes to a shard; it does not automatically create one shard per device. Firehose buffering adds latency and does not provide arbitrary historical replay.','With 3 MB/s writes and 4,500 small records/s, the record-rate limit can require five standard provisioned shards even when bytes alone suggest three.','What do you calculate before choosing shard count?','At least the ceilings for write bytes, write records and read throughput, then account for skew, consumer mode and headroom.')
L(8,491,494,'Amazon MSK & Kafka compatibility','MSK menjalankan managed Apache Kafka. Kafka topics terbagi menjadi partitions; consumers menggunakan offsets.','Choose MSK when Kafka API/client/ecosystem compatibility is a requirement. Provisioned and serverless options have different operational/capacity models.~Messages are ordered within a partition, not across every partition in a topic. Consumer groups coordinate processing; offsets support replay within retention.~Kinesis is AWS-native streaming with shards and its own APIs. Both need thoughtful key distribution, retention, security and consumer design.','Existing Kafka application with minimal API changes: MSK. AWS-native stream without Kafka dependency: compare Kinesis.','Adding partitions can affect key-to-partition mapping and ordering assumptions. Managed Kafka still needs a suitable topic and consumer design.','An existing Kafka telemetry pipeline moves to MSK while retaining compatible producers and Flink processing.','Kafka partition or entire topic: where is order guaranteed?','Within a partition. Cross-partition global ordering requires additional application design.')
L(8,495,500,'Batch: containers for finite jobs','Batch menangani job queue dan compute scheduling. Job bukan service HTTP yang harus selalu hidup.','Package finite jobs as container images and provide job requirements. Batch uses supported compute environments and scales resources to demand.~Managed environments handle underlying capacity choices; unmanaged environments give you greater infrastructure responsibility. EventBridge schedules jobs and Step Functions orchestrates dependencies.~Multi-node parallel jobs run tightly coupled work across supported nodes; their purchasing/environment restrictions differ from ordinary jobs.','Long-running containerized batch workload: Batch. Short event handler: Lambda. Continuously running application: ECS/EKS service.','The standard Lambda 15-minute limit cannot be increased just by adding memory. A Batch job still needs input access, IAM, networking and durable output handling.','A two-hour simulation runs in Batch, stores checkpoints/results in S3 and retries safely if its permitted compute is interrupted.','Why use Batch rather than a permanently idle EC2 cron server?','Managed scheduling and demand-based compute can avoid idle capacity and simplify job orchestration.')
L(8,501,507,'EMR, Glue & the Data Catalog','EMR memberi big-data frameworks; Glue menyiapkan data; Data Catalog menyimpan metadata dataset.','EMR runs frameworks such as Spark/Hadoop with suitable cluster or supported managed execution models. Primary nodes coordinate, core nodes can store HDFS data, and task nodes add processing capacity.~Use durable S3 storage for data that must survive a transient cluster. Spot fits interruption-tolerant compute tasks better than fragile stateful dependencies.~Glue ETL transforms data; crawlers discover schema/partitions; the Glue Data Catalog lets supported analytics services share metadata.','Existing Spark/Hadoop ecosystem control: EMR. Managed ETL and schema cataloging: Glue.','A crawler catalogs metadata; it does not automatically clean every bad record or transform all files. HDFS on a terminated cluster is not your durable archive.','Glue converts raw JSON to partitioned Parquet in S3 and updates a catalog that Athena uses to query the curated dataset.','Data Catalog or S3: which holds the actual dataset?','S3 holds the data objects; the catalog stores table/schema/location metadata.')
L(8,508,514,'Redshift, Spectrum & workload management','Redshift adalah analytical warehouse untuk scans, joins, dan aggregations skala besar, bukan OLTP checkout database.','Columnar storage and parallel execution fit analytics. Provisioned and serverless options exist. Load data using supported bulk/streaming paths; enhanced VPC routing controls relevant COPY/UNLOAD network paths.~Spectrum queries external S3 data using catalog metadata without first loading all of it into warehouse tables.~WLM separates/prioritizes query workloads; concurrency scaling adds eligible query capacity. Cross-Region snapshots and encryption grants support recovery designs.','Repeated complex analytical queries: Redshift. Occasional serverless SQL over S3: Athena. Existing warehouse plus lake query: Spectrum.','A row-by-row transactional workload is not the same as a warehouse workload. The slide’s “Redshift is never serverless” comparison is outdated.','Short executive queries use one workload policy while large overnight analytical queries use another, reducing queue interference.','What problem does WLM address?','It manages query queues/priorities/resources so competing workloads do not all suffer from the same scheduling policy.')
L(8,515,518,'DocumentDB & time-series data','Pilih database sesuai data model dan operations, bukan hanya label “NoSQL”.','DocumentDB supports MongoDB-compatible document use cases, with a compatibility matrix that must be checked before migration. It is not identical to every MongoDB version/feature.~Timestream concepts include timestamped measures, dimensions, retention tiers and time-based queries. Availability differs across Timestream offerings and customer eligibility.~Model the actual reads/writes, retention, consistency, latency and licensing/operations constraints.','JSON document application requiring supported MongoDB compatibility: evaluate DocumentDB. Time-series metrics: evaluate an appropriate time-series offering.','“Compatible” never guarantees every driver feature, query behavior or administrative command is identical. Avoid using dated availability assumptions for new deployments.','Sensor records carry deviceId, timestamp and temperature; retention keeps recent data quickly accessible and older data at lower cost.','What must be checked before a MongoDB-to-DocumentDB migration?','Supported engine/API features, drivers, indexes, queries, data types and application behavior under realistic tests.')
L(8,519,527,'Athena, QuickSight & the analytics pipeline','Athena menjawab SQL; QuickSight menyajikan insights; format dan partitioning menentukan banyak biaya scan.','Athena queries supported data sources, commonly S3 via Glue metadata. Partition pruning, columnar formats and compression reduce unnecessary scans. Avoid many tiny files.~Federated query uses supported connectors to access other sources; results and permissions still require design.~QuickSight analyses are authoring workspaces; dashboards are published views. SPICE provides in-memory imported data, with refresh and access controls such as row/column restrictions where supported.','Ad hoc SQL over logs in S3: Athena. Share business dashboards: QuickSight. Stateful stream processing before storage: Flink.','A dashboard is not a security boundary by itself. Configure data permissions and row/column access; do not assume all viewers should see all source rows.','Convert a 1 TB CSV dataset into partitioned Parquet; a query touching a few columns in one day may scan a small fraction of the original data.','Why does Parquet often reduce Athena cost?','Columnar reading and compression reduce bytes scanned, especially when queries select few columns and partitions.')
L(9,528,532,'CloudWatch metrics, alarms & canaries','Metrics adalah angka sepanjang waktu; alarm mengevaluasi kondisi; canary mencoba perjalanan pengguna.','CloudWatch collects service and custom metrics. Standard EC2 monitoring differs from detailed monitoring; memory/filesystem metrics require suitable agents or custom publishing.~Alarms evaluate metric thresholds or supported expressions and invoke configured actions. Pick the statistic, period, evaluation window and missing-data behavior deliberately.~Synthetics canaries exercise APIs or web flows, identifying functional failures even when CPU and instance health look normal.','Need detect a broken login or checkout: synthetic transaction. Need detect high CPU/queue age: metric alarm.','A green infrastructure metric does not prove the business transaction works. A badly chosen health signal can trigger unnecessary scaling or recovery.','A canary signs in and loads an order page every few minutes; its failure alarm alerts responders before many customers complain.','Which monitoring approach detects a valid HTTP 200 page with a broken purchase flow?','A synthetic workflow that actually exercises and verifies the purchase steps, not just a status-code check.')
L(9,533,539,'CloudWatch Logs: query, filter & stream','Log group mengelompokkan aplikasi; log stream memisahkan producer seperti instance atau container.','Set retention intentionally. Logs Insights supports investigation queries; metric filters convert matching log events into numerical signals for alarms.~Subscriptions send new matching events into supported processing/delivery services. S3 export is a batch process and can lag; it is unsuitable for urgent detection.~Deploy/configure the CloudWatch Agent with Systems Manager and Parameter Store. The agent needs permissions and connectivity.','Near-real-time centralized log processing: subscription. Historical archive export: export task. Count repeated errors: metric filter.','Log retention is not automatically optimized for cost. Exporting to S3 does not guarantee immediate delivery or live incident response.','Application logs → subscription → Firehose → central S3, with a separate low-latency alert path for critical errors.','Metric filter versus Logs Insights?','A metric filter continuously creates metrics from matching new events; Logs Insights queries stored logs for investigation/analysis.')
L(9,540,544,'EventBridge: route events by meaning','Event bus menerima events; rules memilih events; targets menjalankan respons.','Default buses receive supported AWS events. Custom buses carry application events; partner buses integrate supported SaaS events.~Event patterns match event content. Archive/replay supports reprocessing; schema discovery/registry helps producers and consumers agree on structure.~Resource policies control cross-account event publication. The destination action may separately need an execution role or target resource policy.','React to a resource change, schedule work, or centralize cross-account events: EventBridge.','EventBridge routing is not a transaction across all targets. Consumers still need idempotency and a retry/failure design.','A new image event routes to a workflow while security findings route to a responder queue using different rules on the bus.','Does permission to PutEvents automatically authorize a rule to call every target?','No. Target invocation permissions and any execution role must also be configured.')
L(9,545,548,'Tracing & AWS Health','Trace mengikuti satu request melalui banyak services. Health event menjelaskan dampak kejadian AWS pada resources kamu.','Distributed tracing links spans/segments across services to show where latency or errors occur. Instrument applications and give telemetry components the required permissions.~Use supported tracing instrumentation, including OpenTelemetry where appropriate, rather than assuming old SDK/daemon guidance never changes.~AWS Health provides account/resource-specific events; EventBridge can route notifications and remediation workflows. Public service status and account-specific impact are different views.','Slow request spanning API → Lambda → database: tracing. Scheduled maintenance affecting an instance: AWS Health.','CloudWatch aggregates do not automatically reveal which downstream call delayed one request. An AWS Health notification does not diagnose every application bug.','A trace shows most latency inside an external payment API, so increasing EC2 CPU is unlikely to solve the bottleneck.','What does a trace add beyond average Lambda duration?','It can connect the request to downstream operations and reveal which dependency or segment consumed time.')
L(10,549,555,'Elastic Beanstalk & environment deployment','Beanstalk mengelola deployment environment dari application code dengan AWS resources di bawahnya.','A web environment uses an appropriate load-balanced or single-instance topology. A worker environment processes queued background work; long tasks should not block a web request.~You retain responsibility for application configuration, supported platform choices, security and update strategy. Beanstalk simplifies operations but does not remove them.~Blue/green uses separate environments: validate the new one, shift traffic or swap environment URLs, and retain a rollback path.','A supported web application needs managed deployment with infrastructure customization: Beanstalk.','Do not couple the lifetime of production data to a disposable application environment. A DNS swap still has caching/connection behavior.','Web requests enqueue video work; a worker environment processes it independently so user-facing latency stays low.','How do you safely validate a new Beanstalk release before all users see it?','Deploy it to a separate environment, test it, then use the chosen traffic-shift/URL-swap procedure with a rollback plan.')
L(10,556,560,'CodeDeploy: rolling, blue/green & canary','Deployment strategy menentukan seberapa besar blast radius jika release baru bermasalah.','In-place EC2 deployments update existing instances in batches with AppSpec lifecycle hooks. Blue/green supplies a replacement environment and shifts traffic.~Lambda deployments move alias traffic among versions; ECS deployments can create a replacement task set with controlled routing.~Canary tests a small fraction first; linear increases it in steps. Pre/post hooks and CloudWatch alarms can stop or roll back an unhealthy rollout.','Low-risk release with quick reversal: blue/green or canary, provided data/schema changes remain compatible.','Traffic rollback does not automatically reverse a destructive database migration. “Zero downtime” depends on health checks, capacity and compatibility.','Send 10% to Lambda version 2, observe error/latency alarms, then increase or roll back the alias.','Canary versus linear?','Canary starts with a small test fraction then advances; linear increases traffic in repeated increments.')
L(10,561,567,'CloudFormation: lifecycle, drift & StackSets','IaC membuat infrastructure reproducible. Stack lifecycle tetap harus melindungi data penting.','Templates describe resources and relationships. StackSets apply stacks across accounts/Regions; automatic organization deployment supports new accounts.~DeletionPolicy controls resource treatment on stack deletion/removal. UpdateReplacePolicy separately addresses replacement during updates. Drift detection reports supported differences from the template.~Custom resources extend provisioning through handlers. Resource import brings supported existing resources under a stack without recreation, using identifiers and required policy metadata.','Same baseline across many accounts: StackSets. Protect data on deletion: appropriate retention policy. Detect manual changes: drift detection.','Drift detection does not universally fix drift or inspect every property. Retain leaves the resource and its ongoing costs outside the deleted stack.','A production database has deliberate deletion and replacement retention policies; a security baseline is deployed to every new account with StackSets.','Does DeletionPolicy:Retain mean CloudFormation continues managing the resource after stack deletion?','No. The resource remains, but management through that deleted stack ends.')
L(10,568,574,'Service Catalog, SAM & CDK','Service Catalog membatasi pilihan provisioning; SAM mempermudah serverless; CDK menulis IaC dengan bahasa pemrograman.','Service Catalog portfolios expose approved products to authorized users. Launch constraints can provide controlled provisioning permissions.~SAM provides serverless resource abstractions and deployment/testing tooling, building on CloudFormation.~CDK code synthesizes CloudFormation templates; reusable constructs help package infrastructure patterns. The resulting deployed permissions and resources still need review.','Pre-approved self-service infrastructure: Service Catalog. Serverless application templates: SAM. Programmatic infrastructure definitions: CDK.','CDK code is not the application’s running backend by itself. A product catalog is not a replacement for organization-wide guardrails.','Developers launch an approved database product from a portfolio without being given unrestricted infrastructure administrator permissions.','What does CDK synthesize?','CloudFormation templates that describe the infrastructure to deploy.')
L(10,575,582,'Systems Manager & Cloud Map','SSM mengelola mesin melalui agent dan service connectivity; Cloud Map membantu aplikasi menemukan service endpoints.','Run Command executes commands across managed nodes. State Manager maintains desired configuration; Automation orchestrates operations; Patch Manager applies approved baselines within maintenance windows.~Session Manager offers controlled interactive access without opening inbound SSH for ordinary sessions. Managed nodes need an agent, role/activation and network access to required service endpoints.~OpsCenter collects operational issues. Cloud Map registers/discovers resource locations and health through supported DNS/API paths.','Manage many hosts without SSH: Systems Manager. Dynamically discover service endpoints: Cloud Map.','An installed agent alone is insufficient: verify IAM and network access. Port-forwarding/SSH session content is not recorded like ordinary shell session logs.','An ASG termination hook triggers cleanup through an Automation runbook, completes the lifecycle action, then permits termination.','Why might an EC2 instance not appear as an SSM managed node?','Check agent health, instance permissions and connectivity/DNS to required Systems Manager endpoints.')
L(11,583,589,'Cost visibility, tags & recommendations','Tags memberi attribution; reports memberi visibility; recommendation tools membantu menemukan pemborosan.','Activate relevant cost allocation tags so billing reports can use them. Consistent keys/values make cost-center analysis meaningful; tagging tools help find missing tags.~Trusted Advisor provides supported best-practice checks. Compute Optimizer focuses on resource sizing recommendations; Service Quotas manages supported quota visibility and increases.~Current support plans and included features can differ from the old comparison table. Use the current AWS support documentation for plan decisions.','Who spent it: cost allocation and usage reports. Which resource is oversized: Compute Optimizer. Quota approaching limit: Service Quotas/alarms.','A tag existing on a resource is not automatically an activated billing dimension. A recommendation is not proof the proposed size meets peak requirements.','A finance team groups spend by CostCenter and identifies a lightly used instance; operations checks peaks before resizing.','Does Trusted Advisor itself increase a service quota?','No. Use the supported quota-request process; recommendations/monitoring and quota changes are separate.')
L(11,590,591,'Savings Plans & commitment risk','Diskon commitment mengurangi harga usage yang cocok, tetapi kamu membayar commitment meskipun utilization turun.','Compute Savings Plans cover eligible EC2/Fargate/Lambda usage with broad flexibility. EC2 Instance Savings Plans are narrower by family/Region. RIs have service- and scope-specific attributes.~Separate baseline utilization from unpredictable bursts before committing. Eligible excess usage is billed under its applicable pricing, often On-Demand.~Dedicated Hosts address physical tenancy/license requirements; they are not merely a generic discount plan.','Stable flexible compute spend: evaluate Compute Savings Plans. Short interruption-tolerant work: Spot. Uncertain usage: avoid overcommitting.','A one-year discount can cost more overall if you commit to capacity/spend you will not use. Commitment is not a usage ceiling.','If only 40% of a fleet runs continuously, size a commitment against the defensible baseline and handle variable demand separately.','Does a Savings Plan stop resources once its hourly commitment is consumed?','No. Additional eligible usage continues and is billed at the applicable rate.')
L(11,592,601,'S3 economics: access pattern first','Storage termurah per GB belum tentu total cost termurah. Hitung retrieval, requests, transfer, dan minimum durations.','Standard handles frequent access. Standard-IA provides immediate access with retrieval charges. One Zone-IA fits re-creatable data where one-AZ loss is acceptable.~Glacier Instant Retrieval is immediately accessible; Flexible Retrieval and Deep Archive have restore delays. Intelligent-Tiering adapts eligible objects to access patterns, with optional archive tiers that have different retrieval behavior.~Requester Pays shifts eligible request/data-download charges to the requester; the owner still pays storage.','Unknown/changing access: evaluate Intelligent-Tiering. Rare archive with long restore tolerance: Deep Archive. Non-recreatable single copy: avoid relying on one AZ.','Durability measures data survival; availability measures access. A design target, a contractual SLA and observed downtime are not interchangeable.','An auditor needs a file within seconds once a quarter: Glacier Instant Retrieval can fit better than Deep Archive despite higher storage cost.','Why can moving tiny short-lived files to an archive tier increase cost?','Minimum billable size/duration, request overhead and retrieval fees can outweigh the lower storage rate.')
L(11,602,610,'Budgets, Cost Explorer & rightsizing','Budget adalah feedback/control workflow, bukan hard real-time spending cap.','Budgets tracks configured cost/usage/commitment targets and sends notifications. Budget Actions can apply supported policies or stop eligible resources automatically or after approval.~Cost Explorer visualizes trends and forecasts; detailed cost/usage data supports deeper analytics. Central or member-account budget management depends on organizational ownership.~Compute Optimizer uses utilization metrics to suggest configurations. Memory-aware decisions need memory telemetry where required. Discount sharing is configurable across organization accounts.','Need an alert/action on spend threshold: Budgets. Need investigate trend: Cost Explorer. Need detailed line-item analysis: cost/usage exports.','Cost data is delayed. Even automated budget actions cannot guarantee spending never exceeds a threshold. Restrictive actions also need to preserve critical operations.','A development budget alerts the owner early and applies an approved restriction at a higher threshold; production follows a different response policy.','Does a budget notification itself stop EC2?','No. Stopping requires a configured supported Budget Action or another explicitly designed automation.')
L(12,611,616,'The 7 Rs: choose the migration intention','Migration strategy dimulai dari business value, dependencies dan constraints, bukan service favorit.','Retire removes what is unnecessary; retain keeps it for now. Rehost moves largely unchanged; relocate moves to a compatible infrastructure/platform environment.~Replatform introduces limited platform improvements without a full redesign. Repurchase replaces the product, often with SaaS. Refactor/re-architect changes the application design substantially.~Map dependency groups, migration waves, testing, cutover and rollback before executing.','Fastest low-change server migration: rehost. Reduce database operations with limited app changes: replatform to a managed compatible engine.','“Move to cloud” is not always the right outcome for every workload. Percentage cost savings in examples are not universal promises.','Retire an unused report server, retain a constrained mainframe, rehost an urgent app, and later refactor its batch processing.','Database from self-managed MySQL to RDS MySQL: which R?','Typically replatform: the engine/application can remain similar while database infrastructure becomes managed.')
L(12,617,625,'Storage Gateway: file, volume or tape?','Gateway mempertahankan interface yang dikenal aplikasi sambil memakai storage AWS.','S3 File Gateway presents NFS/SMB backed by S3 objects and caches recent data. Coordinate cache refresh when changes occur outside the gateway; independent writers need careful consistency design.~Volume Gateway exposes iSCSI block volumes. Cached mode keeps primary data in AWS with a local cache; stored mode keeps the full local dataset with cloud backups.~Tape Gateway presents a virtual tape library for existing backup software. Lifecycle/archive behavior and restore steps matter.','NFS/SMB-to-S3 hybrid access: File Gateway. iSCSI volumes: Volume Gateway. Existing virtual-tape workflow: Tape Gateway.','S3 File Gateway is not an arbitrary POSIX filesystem over S3 with every locking/consistency behavior. Cloud-side changes may require cache refresh.','A branch reads a read-only file share backed by the same S3 dataset while a primary workflow writes; refresh procedures keep the branch view current.','Cached versus stored Volume Gateway: where is the full primary dataset?','Cached: in AWS with local hot data. Stored: on premises with cloud backups.')
L(12,626,630,'Offline transfer & edge processing','Jika network terlalu lambat, physical data transport bisa lebih cepat—tergantung device availability dan shipping time.','Estimate transfer time using bits/bandwidth and realistic utilization; include protocol overhead and competing traffic. Compare with shipping, loading and import lead times.~The slides describe Snow devices for offline migration and edge compute. Their present ordering eligibility is a separate product-lifecycle issue; do not assume every new customer can order every legacy device.~Improve transfer throughput with parallelism, appropriately batched small files and fewer local-network bottlenecks.','For an exam scenario explicitly offering a supported Snow device and poor connectivity, offline transfer may fit. For a live design, verify current eligibility.','100 Mbps is megabits per second, not megabytes. A theoretical transfer estimate is a lower bound, not an operational schedule.','10 TB at 100 Mbps takes about 9.26 days at perfect utilization; at 75% utilization it takes about 12.35 days, before other overhead.','What assumption most often makes a transfer estimate too optimistic?','Treating line rate as sustained effective throughput and ignoring shared bandwidth, retries and processing time.')
L(12,631,635,'DMS, schema conversion & CDC cutover','Schema conversion mengubah struktur/logic; DMS memindahkan data dan dapat mengikuti perubahan.','Homogeneous migration keeps the engine; heterogeneous migration may need schema conversion and application changes. SCT or supported DMS schema conversion assists, but unsupported objects require manual work.~DMS supports full load, full load plus CDC, or CDC-only for supported source/target pairs. The replication service can use supported provisioned/serverless deployment models.~Validate data, monitor replication lag, pause final writes, catch up, redirect clients and retain a rollback strategy.','Minimum downtime database migration: full load plus CDC with tested cutover. Different engine: add schema/application conversion.','DMS does not automatically convert every stored procedure or guarantee zero downtime. “You must create your own EC2 instance” is an oversimplification of managed replication resources.','Move Oracle data to a compatible Aurora design: assess/convert schema, bulk load, replicate ongoing changes, validate, then cut over.','When is SCT not needed just to change the hosting platform?','When the database engine/schema remains compatible, such as PostgreSQL on premises to RDS PostgreSQL; still assess extensions and compatibility.')
L(12,636,645,'Disaster recovery: RPO vs RTO','RPO = berapa banyak data terbaru boleh hilang. RTO = berapa lama layanan boleh berhenti.','Backup/restore minimizes standing infrastructure but requires restoration. Pilot light keeps essential core/data services ready; much application capacity is not yet serving.~Warm standby runs a reduced but functioning stack that scales after failure. Multi-site/active-active runs serving capacity in multiple sites with much greater data/operations complexity.~Recovery requires identity, keys, configuration, data, capacity, routing and validation—not only a copied database.','Choose the least costly design that meets the stated recovery objectives, then test it end to end.','Multi-AZ availability is not automatically regional disaster recovery. Replication can copy corruption; retain protected recovery points too.','RPO 15 minutes means losing at most roughly the permitted recent data window; RTO one hour means restoring the service within that downtime objective.','Pilot light versus warm standby?','Pilot light keeps critical core components ready but needs more activation. Warm standby already runs the complete service at reduced scale.')
L(12,646,652,'FIS, discovery, MGN & DRS','Discovery menjawab apa yang ada; migration memindahkan; DR menyiapkan pemulihan berulang.','Application discovery captures inventory, utilization and dependencies; Migration Evaluator supports a business case. Dependency information helps sequence migration waves.~Application Migration Service (MGN) supports rehosting servers with staging replication and cutover. Elastic Disaster Recovery (DRS) focuses on ongoing recovery readiness, drills, failover and failback.~Fault Injection Simulator runs controlled failure experiments with defined targets, stop conditions and monitoring.','Move servers permanently: MGN. Keep recovery capability for servers: DRS. Understand dependencies first: discovery.','A replication agent does not prove application recovery works. Validate boot, licenses, network, identity and business transactions in a recovery drill.','A team discovers app/database dependencies, rehosts them in the same wave, tests cutover, and separately maintains DRS for remaining critical on-premises systems.','What is the key difference between MGN and DRS?','Their goal: migration/cutover versus continuous disaster-recovery readiness and recovery operations.')
L(12,653,656,'AWS Backup & immutable recovery points','Backup Plan mengatur apa, kapan, berapa lama, dan ke mana backup disimpan.','AWS Backup centralizes supported backup workloads, schedules, retention, copies and monitoring. Tag-based assignment and organization policies help apply consistent coverage.~Cross-account and cross-Region copies improve isolation where supported; encryption permissions and service-specific feature support must be checked.~Vault Lock offers governance/compliance retention controls. The strongest compliance protection takes effect according to its configured lock process; it is not identical to a freely removable setting.','Many AWS services need centrally governed backups: AWS Backup. EBS-only snapshot lifecycle automation: DLM may be sufficient.','A successful backup job does not prove a successful restore. Test recovery and confirm required keys remain available.','A protected log/backup account receives eligible recovery copies, and scheduled restore tests verify that the data and application can actually be recovered.','Does deleting an encryption key help protect backups?','No. Losing required key access can make encrypted recovery data unusable.')
L(13,657,660,'VPC, CIDR & route decisions','VPC adalah network boundary regional; subnet berada dalam satu AZ. CIDR menentukan ukuran alamat, bukan izin akses.','IPv4 /n contains 2^(32−n) addresses. In an ordinary AWS IPv4 subnet, five addresses are reserved, so /26 leaves 59 assignable addresses.~A public subnet has a route to an Internet Gateway; an IPv4 instance also needs a public IPv4/EIP and permitted traffic to use that internet path.~Routes select destinations by longest-prefix match. Primary/secondary CIDR rules and allowed address ranges are more nuanced than the slide’s claim that all VPC CIDRs are immutable/private-only.','Start troubleshooting with source, destination, forward route, return route and controls on both sides.','All non-RFC1918 addresses are not automatically usable public addresses; reserved ranges exist. The standard 172.16/12 private range is 172.16.0.0/12.','10.0.1.42 matches both 10.0.0.0/16 and 10.0.1.0/24; the /24 is more specific.','Does placing EC2 in a public subnet give it internet automatically?','No. The instance needs an appropriate public address, routes, and security controls that allow the traffic.')
L(13,661,665,'NAT, security groups, NACLs & IPv6','NAT menyediakan outbound path; SG/NACL memfilter traffic; tidak satu pun menggantikan route yang benar.','A conventional zonal public NAT Gateway uses an EIP in a public subnet; private-subnet default routes point to it. Design AZ failure behavior explicitly.~A NAT instance needs source/destination checking disabled and self-managed capacity/HA. SGs are stateful allow-lists on supported interfaces; NACLs are stateless ordered allow/deny rules at subnet boundaries.~For globally routed IPv6, an egress-only IGW permits outbound-initiated connectivity and return traffic. Private IPv6 address options also exist; “all IPv6 is public” is outdated.','Private IPv4 internet egress: NAT path. Private IPv6 outbound-only to IPv6 internet: egress-only IGW.','NAT does not permit arbitrary unsolicited inbound connections. Stateful SG return traffic still has to pass any applicable stateless NACL and route.','HTTPS request leaves on port 443, but a restrictive NACL also needs the appropriate ephemeral return-port path.','Why can adding an SG inbound allow fail to fix a connection?','A route, NACL, endpoint policy, destination listener or return-path requirement can still block it.')
L(13,666,677,'Peering vs Transit Gateway','Peering adalah koneksi berpasangan. Transit Gateway adalah hub routing dengan segmentation melalui route tables.','Peering supports non-overlapping VPC CIDRs with explicit routes; it is non-transitive. A→B and B→C does not create A→C. Peering cannot generally borrow B’s edge gateways.~Transit Gateway connects supported VPC, VPN and other attachments. Association selects the routing table used for incoming attachment traffic; propagation controls which learned routes enter tables.~Separate TGW tables can isolate production and development while sharing approved services. Central egress also needs symmetric routes and proper NAT/inspection paths.','Few simple VPC pairs: peering. Many VPCs/hybrid transit/central egress: TGW.','Adding an attachment does not mean every network should talk to every other. Overlapping CIDRs are a routing problem, not solved by adding more peering.','Prod attachments use a table containing prod and approved shared services; dev routes are absent or blackholed as designed.','What is the difference between TGW association and propagation?','Association chooses the table an attachment uses to route incoming traffic; propagation adds its learned routes to selected tables.')
L(13,678,689,'Endpoints, PrivateLink & private service access','Private connectivity mengatur jalur; IAM dan resource policies tetap mengatur izin.','Gateway endpoints serve S3/DynamoDB through route tables inside the VPC; they cannot simply be extended through peering, TGW, VPN or DX.~Interface endpoints use ENIs/private addresses and security groups. Private DNS lets supported standard service names resolve privately. On-premises clients need routing and suitable DNS resolution.~PrivateLink exposes supported services without full network peering; the classic customer endpoint-service pattern uses a provider NLB. Endpoint policies further restrict allowed access.','Private S3 from EC2 in its VPC: gateway endpoint. On-premises private S3 access via DX: suitable S3 interface endpoint/DNS.','An endpoint policy does not grant permissions missing from IAM/resource policies. Restricting one endpoint does not automatically forbid every alternate access path.','A provider publishes an NLB-backed service; customers create interface endpoints and consume it without sharing all their network routes.','Why can a perfectly routed endpoint request return AccessDenied?','The caller policy, endpoint policy, resource policy or KMS permission can still reject the action.')
L(13,690,702,'Site-to-Site VPN, Client VPN & hybrid routes','Site-to-Site menghubungkan networks; Client VPN menghubungkan pengguna/perangkat.','Managed Site-to-Site VPN uses IPsec tunnels and supported VGW/TGW termination. Customer gateway configuration represents the on-premises side. BGP can exchange routes dynamically.~Use both tunnels and redundant customer-side/network paths where objectives require it. Two tunnels do not eliminate every single point of failure.~Client VPN uses client authentication plus authorization rules, routes and associated networks. Access to peered/transit/on-premises networks needs a complete path and permissions.','Office/data-center network to AWS: Site-to-Site VPN. Employee laptop access: Client VPN.','VPN connectivity does not automatically authorize every destination. Legacy “one VPN per VPC” diagrams are not the only design; TGW provides modern transit options.','An employee uses Client VPN into an access VPC, then approved TGW routes reach a corporate application over hybrid connectivity.','Does BGP encrypt traffic?','No. BGP exchanges routing information; IPsec supplies VPN encryption.')
L(13,703,714,'Direct Connect: VIFs, encryption & resilience','Direct Connect memberi dedicated connectivity. Private bukan otomatis encrypted, dan satu link bukan HA.','Public VIF reaches supported public AWS services. Private VIF reaches VPC resources through suitable VGW/DX gateway design. Transit VIF connects through DX gateway to TGW.~DX gateway supports cross-Region/account connectivity patterns. SiteLink can connect supported DX locations without routing through an AWS Region.~LAG combines compatible connections but shared-location/device failures remain. Use diverse connections/locations and an appropriate backup path. Encryption options depend on design, such as VPN overlays or supported MACsec.','Consistent hybrid bandwidth/private path: DX. Rapid setup/encrypted internet path: VPN. Many VPCs: DX gateway plus TGW as appropriate.','A LAG at one facility does not protect against losing that facility. An under-sized VPN backup may not meet production throughput during a DX outage.','Two independent DX locations protect against location loss; a tested VPN backup offers another path with explicitly understood capacity.','Public VIF means traffic traverses the public internet—true or false?','False. It reaches public AWS service addresses over Direct Connect; “public” describes the destinations, not an ordinary internet transport path.')
L(13,715,719,'Flow Logs & network troubleshooting','Flow Logs adalah metadata koneksi, bukan isi paket atau HTTP request body.','Inspect source/destination addresses, ports, protocol, action and logging status. Query logs in CloudWatch or S3/Athena and identify which interface produced the record.~An ACCEPT says relevant filtering permitted that flow at the recorded point; it does not prove application success or every downstream hop accepted it.~Compare forward and return paths. Stateful SGs and stateless NACLs explain many asymmetric failures, but logs alone may not uniquely identify the rejecting rule.','Need traffic metadata investigation: Flow Logs. Need API caller history: CloudTrail. Need packet payload: another appropriately authorized packet-analysis approach.','Do not infer an unsolicited internet connection reached a private instance just because a NAT-interface log says ACCEPT. Inspect the complete path.','Requests reach the server but responses are rejected at a subnet boundary: examine outbound/return NACL rules and ephemeral ports.','Can Flow Logs tell you the SQL query inside an encrypted database connection?','No. They capture network flow metadata, not decrypted application content.')
L(13,720,723,'Network Firewall & centralized inspection','Inspection hanya berlaku untuk traffic yang benar-benar dirutekan melalui firewall.','AWS Network Firewall supports stateful/stateless filtering and intrusion-prevention capabilities for designed VPC paths. Rules can inspect supported protocols/domains/patterns.~Central inspection architectures use TGW, inspection subnets/endpoints and route tables to cover east-west and north-south traffic. Maintain symmetric flows and correct AZ routing.~Firewall Manager centralizes supported policies; GWLB can support third-party appliance fleets when that is the requirement.','Managed VPC traffic inspection: Network Firewall. Existing third-party inspection appliances: GWLB pattern. HTTP-specific protection: WAF.','Creating a firewall endpoint without updating routes leaves traffic uninspected. Stateful appliances can fail when return traffic takes a different path.','App VPC → TGW → inspection VPC → egress VPC → internet, with corresponding return routes through the intended inspection path.','East-west versus north-south?','East-west is lateral workload/network traffic; north-south crosses an environment boundary, such as internet or on-premises ingress/egress.')
L(14,724,727,'Bedrock: foundation models, RAG & tuning','RAG memberi model konteks saat menjawab; fine-tuning mengubah model melalui training. Jangan samakan keduanya.','Bedrock provides access to supported foundation models and managed generative-AI application capabilities. Model/provider/Region features differ.~Knowledge bases retrieve relevant external content for grounded responses. Agents coordinate tools; guardrails add supported policy/safety checks. Authorization to retrieve data or call a tool still needs explicit design.~Fine-tuning/customization applies only to supported models/configurations. A standard inference call does not imply a private fine-tuned copy of every model is created for you.','Questions over changing company documents: RAG. A supported systematic behavior/style adaptation: evaluate fine-tuning.','Retrieved text is not inherently trustworthy and a model response is not guaranteed correct. Do not grant an agent broad permissions just because the model is managed.','An employee assistant retrieves only documents that employee may access and cites them; tool calls use a narrowly scoped execution identity.','RAG or fine-tuning when a policy document changes daily?','Usually RAG with updated retrieval data, because the information can change without retraining model weights.')
L(14,728,736,'Managed AI: images, speech & language','Pilih dari jenis input dan output, bukan menebak dari nama service.','Rekognition analyzes images/video; Textract specializes in document text/forms/tables. Transcribe turns speech into text; Polly turns text into speech, with lexicons/SSML for pronunciation and prosody.~Translate translates language; Comprehend extracts language insights such as entities/sentiment. Comprehend Medical targets supported clinical-text analysis.~Lex handles conversational intent; Connect manages contact-center workflows. Confidence thresholds and human review help manage uncertain model outputs.','Image labels: Rekognition. Audio transcript: Transcribe. Spoken output: Polly. Translation: Translate. Entities/sentiment: Comprehend.','A confidence score is not proof. Supported languages/features differ, and automatic PII detection may miss data.','A call pipeline uses Connect, Transcribe, Comprehend and an approved response workflow; Lex handles a constrained appointment intent.','Does Polly transcribe a customer’s call?','No. Polly is text-to-speech; Transcribe is speech-to-text.')
L(14,737,741,'SageMaker, Kendra, Personalize & Textract','Custom model development berbeda dari memakai service AI untuk tugas yang sudah umum.','SageMaker AI supports building, training and deploying ML models with model/data operations responsibilities.~Kendra supports enterprise document search across supported sources. Personalize provides recommendation workflows based on relevant interaction/catalog data.~Textract extracts document text and structured elements such as forms/tables; downstream validation converts extraction into reliable business data.','Build a custom predictive model: SageMaker. Enterprise document search: Kendra. Recommendations: Personalize. Invoice extraction: Textract.','Do not train a custom model when a supported managed task service meets the requirement with less effort. Extraction alone does not validate invoice arithmetic.','Textract reads an invoice; application rules validate totals; ambiguous fields go to human review before accounting approval.','Kendra or Personalize for recommending the next product?','Personalize. Kendra is focused on retrieving information from indexed enterprise content.')
L(15,742,749,'CI/CD: source, build, approve, deploy','CI menguji integrasi perubahan. Continuous delivery menjaga software siap dirilis; deployment policy menentukan kapan release berjalan.','CodePipeline orchestrates stages. CodeBuild compiles/tests/packages. CodeDeploy handles supported deployments; CloudFormation provisions infrastructure. ECR stores container images.~Connect source repositories through supported connections/integrations. Add manual approvals where governance requires a human gate.~Build once, promote the tested artifact, protect credentials and restrict pipeline roles. Security scanning does not replace least privilege or secret rotation.','Need coordinate source→test→approval→deployment: CodePipeline. Need run tests/build image: CodeBuild.','A passing unit test is not proof of production compatibility. The deck’s “CodeBuild has no time limit” should not be memorized as a universal quota claim.','A pipeline tests code, builds an immutable image, pushes it to ECR, waits for production approval and deploys it with monitored rollback.','Does CodePipeline itself compile your application?','It orchestrates a build action such as CodeBuild; the build service performs compilation/tests.')
L(15,750,752,'Contact flows & video streams','Video stream dan metadata event stream mempunyai fungsi dan consumers berbeda.','Kinesis Video Streams ingests/stores supported video streams for playback/processing. Video producers and parser/consumer integrations differ from ordinary Kinesis Data Streams.~A video-analysis pipeline can produce detection metadata into a data stream for analytics, without treating raw video as ordinary tiny event records.~Lex and Connect provide conversational/contact-center workflows. Some adjacent products pictured in older diagrams have retired or changed; focus on the current supported components.','Need ingest camera video: Kinesis Video Streams. Need stream small detection events: Kinesis Data Streams.','A video-stream service does not automatically export every raw clip to your own S3 bucket in the shown pattern. Design the required extraction/archive path.','Cameras send video; analysis emits event metadata; dashboards aggregate detections without repeatedly scanning all video bytes.','Why keep detection metadata separate from raw video?','It makes real-time event processing/search smaller and faster while video retention/playback follows its own storage workflow.')
L(15,753,759,'WorkSpaces, AppStream & Device Farm','Desktop, application streaming, dan testing devices adalah tiga kebutuhan berbeda.','WorkSpaces provides managed virtual desktop experiences with identity/network and lifecycle choices. Availability/DR needs user-state and directory planning, not just an alternate endpoint.~AppStream 2.0 streams supported applications to users, commonly through a browser, reducing client installation requirements.~Device Farm tests applications on supported real devices/browsers and produces testing evidence. WorkSpaces IP access controls restrict permitted connection sources.','Managed employee desktop: WorkSpaces. Stream a specific desktop application: AppStream. Cross-device app testing: Device Farm.','Older WorkSpaces diagrams may reference retired components such as WorkDocs/WAM. Treat them as historical; validate current persistence/application-management choices.','A contractor needs one GPU application from a browser: AppStream may fit better than providing a full persistent employee desktop.','Which service helps test a mobile app on real devices?','AWS Device Farm.')
L(15,760,763,'Macie, SES & campaign messaging','Macie mencari sensitive data di S3; SES mengirim email; campaign orchestration memilih audience dan journey.','Macie inspects supported S3 data for sensitive information and reports findings; it is not a universal scanner for every database.~SES supports transactional/bulk email workflows, deliverability feedback and authentication mechanisms such as DKIM/SPF. Configuration sets route events/metrics and organize sending behavior.~The slides describe Pinpoint for targeted campaigns. Product lifecycle and successor choices must be checked before a new design. SNS and SES alone do not supply every campaign-management feature.','Sensitive-data discovery in S3: Macie. Application email: SES. Event fan-out: SNS.','Finding PII does not automatically redact or delete it. Sending an email is not the same as designing a segmented customer campaign.','SES sends a receipt; a configuration-set event records delivery/bounce information; the application updates contact status through its approved workflow.','Macie or Inspector for credit-card numbers in S3 documents?','Macie. Inspector targets supported workload vulnerabilities rather than document PII discovery.')
L(15,764,768,'Image Builder & IoT Core','Image Builder membuat machine/container image yang diuji; IoT Core menerima device messages dan merutekannya.','Image Builder pipelines build, test and distribute approved AMIs/images across supported accounts/Regions. Rollout to existing instances still needs a deployment/refresh step.~IoT Core provides device connectivity, authentication, publish/subscribe messaging and rules that send data to supported services.~Separate device identity, ingestion, transformation, storage and analytics. Device-side buffering/offline behavior remains part of the application design.','Repeated golden-AMI maintenance: Image Builder. Fleet of connected device messages: IoT Core.','Creating a new AMI does not update every running EC2 instance. An IoT rule does not eliminate downstream quotas or error handling.','IoT messages route into Firehose for S3 storage; a separate Image Builder pipeline patches and validates the analytics worker AMI.','How does a new AMI reach existing ASG instances?','Update the launch template and perform a controlled instance refresh or other deployment process.')
L(16,769,787,'Sample cases: governance, vendor roles & CORS','Tiga pola awal: hormati account autonomy, gunakan machine roles, dan pahami browser cross-origin checks.','Slides 771–776 choose billing alerts under the constraint that business groups retain control. Alerts improve detection; they do not enforce a hard spending cap.~Slides 777–783 use StackSets to place vendor-trusted roles in each required account. A single role in the management account does not automatically confer access to all member resources.~Slides 784–787 require the browser-facing API to permit the page’s origin. The source’s static-website setup is one hosting architecture, not the only way S3 objects can serve a page.','Read the exact question constraints before applying a general best practice from another scenario.','These are supplied worked examples, not evidence of questions on your actual exam. Some old explanations simplify or overstate current behavior.','Explain why “put all IAM users in a group” misses roles/root and why a vendor should assume scoped roles instead of sharing a workforce password.','What two permission relationships matter for vendor cross-account monitoring?','The vendor must be allowed to assume each target role, and each target role needs the necessary read permissions; include a suitable ExternalId condition.')
L(16,788,805,'Sample cases: diagnosis, SSM & role placement','Pisahkan symptom dari root cause. Letakkan role pada account tempat izin itu perlu dijalankan.','Slides 788–794 associate burst failures with Lambda concurrency among their choices. In real diagnosis, a 502 does not uniquely identify throttling: inspect invocation errors, malformed responses and integration logs.~Slides 795–800 select Systems Manager to administer a fleet without opening extra inbound SSH ports.~Slides 801–805 place the production role in the production account, trust an authorized source, and let only operators assume it. IAM groups do not contain users from another account.','Use the evidence supplied by a scenario, but do not memorize “502 always means increase concurrency.”','An admin role in the wrong account does not move its permissions to a different account. Trust policy and identity permissions are complementary.','Developers operate only in Dev; operators share the same home identity but assume a production role when approved.','Why is Run Command compatible with blocked inbound SSH?','The managed agent communicates with Systems Manager through outbound service connectivity, with suitable IAM permissions.')
L(16,806,818,'Sample cases: bottlenecks & modernization','Scaling satu tier dapat merusak tier berikutnya. Hitung demand lalu lindungi bottleneck.','Slides 806–810 replace mostly idle workers with Lambda and consolidate stream capacity within per-shard peak limits. Remember that partition keys hash into shards, not one automatic shard per device.~Slides 811–814 buffer affiliate requests with SQS and constrain consumer concurrency. An asynchronous Lambda call alone can still overwhelm the affiliate.~Slides 815–818 choose managed database/load-balancing improvements while respecting Windows/Arm compatibility. The source skips the label “Question 9”; pages are not missing here.','Protect downstream limits with queues and concurrency/rate control; modernize toward managed services when constraints allow.','Concurrency is not a precise requests-per-second limiter if durations vary. Use explicit rate limiting when the downstream contract is rate-based.','If each worker takes 0.5 s and sends one request, concurrency 10 implies about 20 requests/s on average—not a strict upper-bound SLA.','Why does adding Lambda between a scalable app and an external API not automatically solve overload?','Lambda can scale too. Add a buffer and deliberately bound processing rate/concurrency to the dependency’s capacity.')
L(16,819,828,'Final revision & readiness','Selesai membaca bukan sama dengan bisa menjawab. Readiness terlihat dari recall, explanation, dan timed practice.','Use the seven-day route for a complete content pass, then spend the remaining days on mixed scenarios, error review and a realistic timed practice session.~For every mistake, record whether it came from missing knowledge, misread constraints, calculation, or choosing a working but less suitable option.~Certification-path slides are career context, not a reason to learn unrelated certifications during the last days before this exam. Prioritize weak mechanisms in this deck.','Aim to explain a choice and reject its closest alternative without notes. Use fresh official practice to assess readiness.','The site’s XP and raw practice percentage are learning indicators, not AWS scaled scores or a guarantee of passing.','Before the exam, redraw cross-account trust, hybrid DNS, a queue-buffered service and a DR plan from memory.','What should you write in a mistake note?','The decisive constraint, the correct mechanism, why your chosen option failed, and one cue that will help you recognize the pattern next time.')
